00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:13.326
in his disclosure forms

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:14.260
that he received

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.562
the unemployment insurance checks

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:18.598
and he apparently didn't

00:08:18.598 --> 00:08:19.398
either he did or did

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:21.200
not communicate with donors and say,

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.269
Oh, you give me $25,000.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:24.704
I put it into political advertising,

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:26.639
but instead he funnels it through

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:28.140
and then pays for luxury goods.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:28.508
So.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:28.908
So, Karen,

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:29.475
what is this thing

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:31.244
that I mean, McCarthy in a sense.

00:08:31.244 --> 00:08:31.711
In a sense,

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:32.612
he doesn't really have a choice.

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:33.346
If the Ethics Committee

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:35.348
was going to come out and say guilty,

00:08:35.348 --> 00:08:37.250
he was going to have to probably call

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:37.950
for resignation anyway.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.285
But he comes out and says this.

00:08:39.285 --> 00:08:40.019
That, of course, would

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:41.053
then force a special election

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:42.221
his money was laying out.

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:43.322
This is a swing district.

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:45.725
It's a predominantly Democratic

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:48.127
district that for various reasons right.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:48.394
It was

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:50.229
it was more about the policies

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:51.397
they wanted than it was about George

00:08:51.397 --> 00:08:52.899
Santos himself.

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:54.333
It's a risky, special election.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.435
McCarthy only has, as many said,

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:57.970
four seats he can afford to lose.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:58.371
That's right.

00:08:58.371 --> 00:08:59.972
It would be incredibly risky.

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:01.207
And I do think actually

00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:02.475
a Democrat would win.

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:03.576
It's as you mentioned, it's

00:09:03.576 --> 00:09:04.877
a heavily Democratic district.

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:06.445
I think many in the district

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:07.613
just really weren't taking it

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:09.815
very seriously, if I'm being honest.

00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:12.351
So but now the stakes are much higher.

00:09:12.552 --> 00:09:13.920
It's not surprising.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:14.487
It's you know, it's

00:09:14.487 --> 00:09:15.588
relatively easy

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:17.123
for McCarthy to come out and say

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:17.657
that he wouldn't

00:09:17.657 --> 00:09:19.191
support him for reelection

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:21.193
because the truth is he needs him now.

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:22.628
I mean, you heard Santos

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:23.462
when he left the courtroom

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:24.530
to talk about how he wanted

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:26.499
to get back to vote on the border, Bill.

00:09:26.499 --> 00:09:27.033
So it's

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:28.901
that those pieces of legislation

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:31.003
that McCarthy is trying to get through,

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:31.771
that he is

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:34.607
using as part of his negotiations

00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:36.475
or, you know, messaging against Biden,

00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:37.910
he needs them and needs those votes.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.512
But it puts the urgency of this

00:09:39.512 --> 00:09:40.646
front and center, Scott,

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:41.981
over vote margin.

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:44.183
And this is something that could play out

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:46.085
again, as the ambassador was saying

00:09:46.085 --> 00:09:47.286
before we came to air

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.754
The Ethics Committee is very secretive.

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:49.922
You don't know where they are

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:50.756
in their process,

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:52.758
but that could come relatively quickly

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:53.426
and then all of a sudden,

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:55.328
boom, special election. Yeah.

00:09:55.328 --> 00:09:57.163
And it would be very competitive

00:09:57.163 --> 00:09:58.297
I don't know

00:09:58.297 --> 00:09:59.432
who the Democrats would nominate

00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:00.633
or who the Republicans would put up,

00:10:00.633 --> 00:10:01.267
but I suspect

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:03.202
both parties would be all in on it.

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:05.037
I mean, a Republican did win here,

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:06.072
even though people weren't

00:10:06.072 --> 00:10:07.106
paying a ton of attention

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:09.075
and I don't think Biden is getting any

00:10:09.075 --> 00:10:10.109
more popular by the day.

00:10:10.109 --> 00:10:11.043
So I think it would be

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:12.178
a very competitive race.

00:10:12.178 --> 00:10:14.013
But this is the wages,

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:14.747
by the way,

00:10:14.747 --> 00:10:16.082
of not doing as well in the midterm

00:10:16.082 --> 00:10:17.350
as we should have

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:18.517
you know, the margins shouldn't be that

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:19.452
you don't have margin.

00:10:19.452 --> 00:10:21.020
You don't have the margin. That's right.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.688
And that's something

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:23.823
this should come to

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:24.924
no surprise to anyone.

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:26.425
The policy is, Scott said,

00:10:26.425 --> 00:10:29.095
and the attorneys, the professor said

00:10:29.295 --> 00:10:30.963
they're spot on that legals

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:32.398
playing its role.

00:10:32.398 --> 00:10:32.865
Obviously,

00:10:32.865 --> 00:10:34.867
the Ethics Committee is playing its role.

00:10:34.867 --> 00:10:35.701
But listen,

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:36.969
there's plenty of blame to go around

00:10:36.969 --> 00:10:38.170
